1
00:00:04,735 --> 00:02:05,765
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:08,835 --> 00:02:13,355
EPISODE 83

3
00:02:17,835 --> 00:02:23,845
A time had come, brother, where
our paths departed.

4
00:02:26,115 --> 00:02:28,135
You who were on the path of justice...

5
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:32,295
...and me who had a blind eye.

6
00:02:33,855 --> 00:02:35,385
I made mistake.

7
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,205
I became unwary.

8
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:41,305
My blood is halal to you my brother.

9
00:02:44,815 --> 00:02:46,395
Come on, brother.

10
00:02:48,365 --> 00:02:49,745
Come on.

11
00:04:26,515 --> 00:04:32,255
The only way appears to be on
the edge of my weapon, my Shiekh.

12
00:04:32,735 --> 00:04:34,275
That is right.

13
00:04:34,995 --> 00:04:37,035
It's on the edge of your weapon.

14
00:04:37,245 --> 00:04:43,365
But it's not the weapon on your belly...

15
00:04:45,015 --> 00:04:47,045
...that will wake Gündüz from sleep.

16
00:04:48,435 --> 00:04:51,625
It's the mercy in your heart.

17
00:04:52,155 --> 00:04:53,855
It's to forgive.

18
00:04:55,975 --> 00:04:58,995
Even if he has done all of these things?

19
00:05:00,895 --> 00:05:05,115
Human nature is tendentious
to make mistakes.

20
00:05:05,535 --> 00:05:06,875
We're human beings.

21
00:05:08,175 --> 00:05:11,435
The important thing is regretting.

22
00:05:12,265 --> 00:05:17,155
Regretting and asking
Allah for forgiveness.

23
00:05:18,945 --> 00:05:22,025
Do not preserve your
mercy from someone who...

24
00:05:22,795 --> 00:05:25,535
...asks Allah for mercy.

25
00:05:27,135 --> 00:05:28,655
Forgiving...

26
00:05:29,855 --> 00:05:32,895
...is the tradition of Allah.

27
00:05:37,185 --> 00:05:39,245
Let the government you dream of...

28
00:05:39,965 --> 00:05:44,305
...grow with not only its
strength but with its mercy.

29
00:05:47,385 --> 00:05:49,905
Forgive your brother.

30
00:05:52,625 --> 00:05:55,155
One day, death will find us all.

31
00:05:57,215 --> 00:06:00,115
But I will not take your life today.

32
00:06:04,755 --> 00:06:06,785
You beg Allah.

33
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:11,495
So that he can forgive you.

34
00:06:15,455 --> 00:06:19,005
I got set up in a dirty scheme, brother.

35
00:06:21,765 --> 00:06:23,855
When I wanted to do good...

36
00:06:26,035 --> 00:06:30,275
...I became the tool of the tyrants.

37
00:06:31,055 --> 00:06:33,095
If you can see that you fell...

38
00:06:34,535 --> 00:06:37,275
...then why don't you stand up, brother?

39
00:06:40,815 --> 00:06:43,835
Why do you send the alps to Geyhatu?

40
00:06:44,115 --> 00:06:47,295
Why do you try to destroy
the Turkmen tribes?

41
00:06:48,175 --> 00:06:50,395
I knew you would be in my way, Osman.

42
00:06:53,555 --> 00:06:55,095
I knew it.

43
00:06:57,895 --> 00:06:59,395
I would pray...

44
00:07:01,135 --> 00:07:03,325
...something would happen
to me on the road...

45
00:07:04,515 --> 00:07:06,705
...so that I could not
achieve my objective.

46
00:07:07,185 --> 00:07:08,535
Look,...

47
00:07:09,365 --> 00:07:11,465
...my prayer was not unanswered, brother.

48
00:07:12,025 --> 00:07:13,615
It came true.

49
00:07:15,175 --> 00:07:18,895
Your intent and action
are different, brother.

50
00:07:20,505 --> 00:07:27,595
Geyhatu was going to burn the monastery,
the willow, and the entire tent.

51
00:07:30,635 --> 00:07:32,425
To stop him...

52
00:07:33,055 --> 00:07:34,755
...to stop him...

53
00:07:36,695 --> 00:07:38,575
...I gave Geyhatu a promise.

54
00:07:38,785 --> 00:07:40,315
No Kayı,...

55
00:07:40,975 --> 00:07:42,485
...no monastery...

56
00:07:43,145 --> 00:07:44,675
...no willow...

57
00:07:46,935 --> 00:07:49,935
...they don't stand against martyrdom.

58
00:07:52,695 --> 00:07:55,225
But just because they could live...

59
00:07:56,875 --> 00:07:58,915
...you did not care for them.

60
00:08:05,175 --> 00:08:07,435
I made a lot of mistakes, brother.

61
00:08:09,335 --> 00:08:10,675
A lot.

62
00:08:15,555 --> 00:08:17,335
I can't count.

63
00:08:18,815 --> 00:08:20,345
There are so many.

64
00:08:28,135 --> 00:08:30,405
İNEGÖL CASTLE

65
00:08:32,755 --> 00:08:37,604
Mingiyan. Mongols came to my
castle a bunch of times before.

66
00:08:38,575 --> 00:08:40,083
Yet,...

67
00:08:41,234 --> 00:08:43,765
...Osman killed them every time.

68
00:08:44,775 --> 00:08:47,405
But now, we're friends.

69
00:08:47,405 --> 00:08:49,795
We're together against Osman, right?

70
00:08:49,945 --> 00:08:53,075
Geyhatu warned me about you.

71
00:08:53,415 --> 00:08:58,475
Don't be afraid if he draws his
weapon but be afraid if he speaks.

72
00:09:00,075 --> 00:09:01,875
So, shut up Nikola.

73
00:09:05,835 --> 00:09:09,705
"Don't be afraid if he draws his weapon
but be afraid if he speaks." That's nice.

74
00:09:09,945 --> 00:09:12,055
Geyhatu is a good judge of character.

75
00:09:12,375 --> 00:09:16,725
Nikola, I will see your
soldiers, swords, horses...

76
00:09:17,495 --> 00:09:21,345
I will review the army
you'll give to Geyhatu.

77
00:09:21,595 --> 00:09:24,335
You'll do all of this
Mingiyan, I mean all of it.

78
00:09:24,535 --> 00:09:28,575
But before that, I got
a little surprise for you.

79
00:09:29,895 --> 00:09:31,195
Soldier!

80
00:09:40,555 --> 00:09:43,045
Coghatuz

81
00:09:49,435 --> 00:09:50,995
Nikola,

82
00:09:53,045 --> 00:09:57,315
I knew you were not trustworthy.

83
00:09:57,665 --> 00:10:00,115
You know everything Logotuz

84
00:10:00,715 --> 00:10:03,595
Maybe you know where Osman is as well.

85
00:10:33,215 --> 00:10:36,045
I will not punish you today.

86
00:10:38,515 --> 00:10:41,405
You will obey me.

87
00:10:43,695 --> 00:10:45,975
You'll do whatever I ask.

88
00:11:06,035 --> 00:11:08,135
I am at your command Osman Bey.

89
00:11:12,515 --> 00:11:15,315
Don't you get this out of your head.

90
00:11:17,245 --> 00:11:20,295
No one will know.

91
00:11:21,635 --> 00:11:25,025
You'll keep commanding
like a bey at the tent.

92
00:11:29,115 --> 00:11:32,135
I will kill the ones...

93
00:11:32,715 --> 00:11:36,275
...who had tricked you.

94
00:11:39,295 --> 00:11:41,645
You will bring me Geyhatu.

95
00:11:42,295 --> 00:11:44,905
I will get on his neck like a wolf.

96
00:11:49,915 --> 00:11:52,165
Now you go to him...

97
00:11:54,555 --> 00:11:56,705
...so that he doesn't figure out our plan.

98
00:11:58,525 --> 00:12:00,575
May Allah bless you, my brother!

99
00:12:02,235 --> 00:12:03,575
May Allah bless you!

100
00:12:18,175 --> 00:12:19,545
Horses!

101
00:12:24,955 --> 00:12:26,735
Go back to the tent!

102
00:12:28,515 --> 00:12:34,305
Today, the blood of the tyrant
will shed, not the Turks'.

103
00:13:55,695 --> 00:13:58,575
Just the way I want.

104
00:14:08,495 --> 00:14:12,025
So, you're not going to speak now?

105
00:14:15,435 --> 00:14:17,935
Alright, suit yourself.

106
00:14:21,055 --> 00:14:22,115
No!

107
00:14:28,885 --> 00:14:32,635
I like burning people.

108
00:14:47,555 --> 00:14:50,815
Even if I gave you Osman's location,
you would still kill me.

109
00:14:52,075 --> 00:14:53,599
If Osman lives...

110
00:14:54,075 --> 00:14:57,615
...we'll have a chance to
get vengeance on you.

111
00:14:58,255 --> 00:15:02,295
Do you see how he trusts Osman?

112
00:15:02,815 --> 00:15:06,955
If you speak, you may stay alive.

113
00:15:08,735 --> 00:15:10,055
Isn't that right?

114
00:15:10,055 --> 00:15:12,055
What we need is Osman's location...

115
00:15:12,055 --> 00:15:18,595
This fool can live the
rest of his life stamped.

116
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,140
Come on!

117
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:24,920
Tell us Osman's location, come on!

118
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,960
You wanted this.

119
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:34,900
Alright, alright, alright!

120
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:37,820
Alright, alright, alright!
I'll tell you!

121
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:43,600
Osman and Koses are
hiding at Kuzgun Hill.

122
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:52,000
Huh, now you gave us
the information we wanted.

123
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:55,280
Untie him. Untie him.

124
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:23,020
I got one more surprise for you.

125
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:45,180
I knew you would do this.

126
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,138
You know everything but...

127
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,500
...do it anyways.

128
00:17:07,638 --> 00:17:09,780
You are an ignoble man, Nikola.

129
00:17:10,118 --> 00:17:11,940
And always live that way.

130
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:13,940
But, I will live.

131
00:17:19,419 --> 00:17:21,000
Soldier!

132
00:17:35,135 --> 00:17:36,455
That's it!

133
00:17:37,115 --> 00:17:39,675
Geyhatu likes this.

134
00:17:44,395 --> 00:17:45,695
Argus!

135
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:47,355
Get an army with you!

136
00:17:47,735 --> 00:17:49,495
I want Koses and Osman!

137
00:18:01,575 --> 00:18:02,935
Hold!

138
00:18:03,455 --> 00:18:06,455
My bey, I waited at
Kurtboğazı as you wished.

139
00:18:06,595 --> 00:18:08,475
They found me and gave me your deposit.

140
00:18:27,275 --> 00:18:31,095
Beys inform us that they
have accepted our invitation.

141
00:18:31,095 --> 00:18:32,415
Thank Allah!

142
00:18:32,515 --> 00:18:34,515
Praise be!

143
00:18:36,475 --> 00:18:40,295
Now go and prepare for a feast

144
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:42,875
Now,...

145
00:18:43,295 --> 00:18:46,435
...now we're going to flare up
the fire of rebellion inside them.

146
00:18:46,715 --> 00:18:52,235
Weapons will not be in their
holsters until these lands are revived!

147
00:18:53,255 --> 00:18:59,275
Geyhatu will regret not
coming but being born.

148
00:18:59,355 --> 00:19:00,735
Come on!

149
00:19:24,835 --> 00:19:26,215
Kumral!

150
00:19:26,595 --> 00:19:27,935
Hide!

151
00:19:30,355 --> 00:19:31,915
Allah, Allah!

152
00:20:18,015 --> 00:20:24,055
Master Davut, I did not think
it would be this powerful.

153
00:20:24,275 --> 00:20:26,175
Not only did it explode...

154
00:20:27,055 --> 00:20:30,255
...but I also put the parts remaining
from the weapons inside.

155
00:20:32,315 --> 00:20:34,995
They'll stick on the ones
around it like arrows.

156
00:20:34,995 --> 00:20:37,535
Those damn Geyhatu dogs.

157
00:20:40,715 --> 00:20:43,235
Before those dogs, you
were going to get me!

158
00:20:43,675 --> 00:20:44,995
Did you plan this?

159
00:20:45,095 --> 00:20:46,535
That's right Kumral Abdal

160
00:20:47,235 --> 00:20:48,855
It's a really good plan.

161
00:20:50,855 --> 00:20:54,855
It will drop a bunch of them without
even drawing our weapons.

162
00:21:02,595 --> 00:21:04,575
Shepherd is a dervish.

163
00:21:07,215 --> 00:21:09,355
Does a dervish ever stay out of trouble?

164
00:21:10,155 --> 00:21:11,515
Of course not.

165
00:21:13,275 --> 00:21:17,175
Shepherd's seclusion is because
of his preparedness for war.

166
00:21:49,835 --> 00:21:51,875
Instead of throwing this with its fuse...

167
00:21:55,235 --> 00:21:56,975
...can we throw it with a catapult?

168
00:21:57,595 --> 00:21:58,935
But,...

169
00:21:58,995 --> 00:22:01,495
...what if it explodes the moment it hits.

170
00:22:05,175 --> 00:22:08,215
It would do damage ten times
more than a cannon can.

171
00:22:11,695 --> 00:22:16,775
But it needs power for it to
explode the moment it hits.

172
00:22:22,395 --> 00:22:23,955
I'll look out for that.

173
00:22:26,395 --> 00:22:27,935
I'll look out for that.

174
00:22:31,795 --> 00:22:33,315
Praise be!

175
00:22:33,515 --> 00:22:35,515
He won't leave a wall not demolished.

176
00:22:43,155 --> 00:22:44,875
We'll not just demolish them...

177
00:22:45,975 --> 00:22:48,015
...if we're going to demolish a wall...

178
00:22:49,735 --> 00:22:51,735
...we'll build inside.

179
00:22:52,355 --> 00:22:54,075
If we're going to demolish a wall...

180
00:22:54,895 --> 00:22:56,935
...we'll revive it.

181
00:23:00,595 --> 00:23:03,675
Also, what is demolishing for?

182
00:23:07,395 --> 00:23:09,475
To build back better.

183
00:23:11,535 --> 00:23:13,075
I'll look for it.

184
00:23:13,755 --> 00:23:15,255
I'll look for it.

185
00:23:16,035 --> 00:23:17,575
I'll look for it.

186
00:23:49,015 --> 00:23:54,055
A man without hands is
prey to the animals in nature.

187
00:23:56,875 --> 00:24:01,375
This is what the fools who
cannot protect the fire deserve.

188
00:24:03,235 --> 00:24:08,315
It seems Rogatus was
not a man, just like them.

189
00:24:08,875 --> 00:24:11,575
He could not endure the torture.

190
00:24:12,355 --> 00:24:15,255
He said where Osman will be.

191
00:24:16,295 --> 00:24:19,135
Where will Osman's head be?

192
00:24:19,575 --> 00:24:22,015
Osman had kept changing his location...

193
00:24:22,015 --> 00:24:26,555
...but he has a meeting with
Rogatus tomorrow night.

194
00:24:28,415 --> 00:24:30,455
He'll be at Kuzgun hill.

195
00:24:31,055 --> 00:24:33,075
Make your preparations Mingiyan.

196
00:24:33,335 --> 00:24:36,915
Kuzgun Hill will be hell for Osman.

197
00:24:37,415 --> 00:24:39,935
Yes, Commander Geyhatu!

198
00:24:42,415 --> 00:24:44,655
Gündüz Bey is here, Commander Geyhatu.

199
00:24:44,655 --> 00:24:47,075
But he is alone. Doesn't
have his alps with him.

200
00:24:48,495 --> 00:24:49,875
Let him come.

201
00:24:50,355 --> 00:24:51,655
Yes, sir!

202
00:24:52,675 --> 00:24:54,375
Where are the alps?

203
00:24:55,635 --> 00:25:00,635
How could Gündüz come to
me without keeping his word?

204
00:25:11,395 --> 00:25:17,485
My bey, as you wished, I shifted some
of the Seljuk soldiers behind the tent.

205
00:25:18,235 --> 00:25:21,335
But the ones in the
entrance will not move.

206
00:25:26,915 --> 00:25:29,295
You got one more duty Erdu Alp.

207
00:25:30,775 --> 00:25:32,295
When the night falls...

208
00:25:32,955 --> 00:25:37,315
...get as many Seljuk soldiers
out of the tent as you can.

209
00:25:38,235 --> 00:25:40,015
We'll handle the rest.

210
00:25:40,435 --> 00:25:41,975
Yes, my bey!

211
00:25:49,055 --> 00:25:50,415
My bey,...

212
00:25:51,655 --> 00:25:53,835
...will we trust Güzdüz Bey?

213
00:26:02,135 --> 00:26:04,155
Punishment of treachery is clear.

214
00:26:07,195 --> 00:26:08,935
If he betrays us...

215
00:26:11,415 --> 00:26:12,955
...he'll pay the price.

216
00:26:34,695 --> 00:26:37,755
Circumstances of traitors
are clear, Gündüz.

217
00:26:41,315 --> 00:26:43,015
You did it with your hands...

218
00:26:43,335 --> 00:26:45,335
...and pay it with your neck.

219
00:26:49,015 --> 00:26:52,895
Osman will make you pay for
what you have done eventually.

220
00:27:08,595 --> 00:27:11,115
Will you be Abel or Cain?

221
00:27:11,655 --> 00:27:13,565
Will you turn your back on your brother?

222
00:27:20,435 --> 00:27:24,995
If you side with Geyhatu, power,
office, position will be yours.

223
00:27:46,235 --> 00:27:48,315
Where are my Alps, Gündüz?

224
00:27:49,375 --> 00:27:51,435
Alps are a whole, Geyhatu

225
00:27:52,235 --> 00:27:53,755
Where are they?

226
00:27:56,415 --> 00:27:57,775
At the tent.

227
00:27:59,555 --> 00:28:02,215
You were going to bring your alps...

228
00:28:02,735 --> 00:28:05,875
...army was going to head
towards lord castles.

229
00:28:14,015 --> 00:28:16,575
Why are alps at the tent, Gündüz?

230
00:28:21,735 --> 00:28:23,475
I know Osman,..

231
00:28:24,415 --> 00:28:27,745
...I keep them at the tent for the
possibility of a raid on the road.

232
00:28:28,535 --> 00:28:31,225
The weapons of my alps
will spill blood for you Geyhatu.

233
00:28:32,435 --> 00:28:34,055
Be sure of that.

234
00:28:34,875 --> 00:28:39,955
Following my orders will keep
all of you alive Gündüz Bey.

235
00:28:40,135 --> 00:28:45,095
Or I'll burn all of you alive.

236
00:28:47,475 --> 00:28:49,255
I gave you a word...

237
00:28:49,295 --> 00:28:50,875
...and I'll keep it.

238
00:28:51,255 --> 00:28:53,255
Have no doubt.

239
00:28:53,735 --> 00:28:56,255
I don't doubt...

240
00:28:57,575 --> 00:28:59,595
...I destroy!

241
00:29:07,735 --> 00:29:09,755
What about Osman?

242
00:29:11,495 --> 00:29:13,555
Is there any word from him?

243
00:29:23,235 --> 00:29:25,295
Osman is cautious.

244
00:29:26,355 --> 00:29:28,505
He stays at a different
location each night.

245
00:29:28,755 --> 00:29:30,755
But I'm very close, I'll find him

246
00:29:30,755 --> 00:29:35,015
Then don't stay here, go and find Osman...

247
00:29:35,015 --> 00:29:39,755
...and when I want your
alps, bring them here!

248
00:29:42,835 --> 00:29:44,375
May Allah bless you, Geyhatu!

249
00:29:45,155 --> 00:29:46,675
I'll do what you say.

250
00:29:54,255 --> 00:30:01,305
No one lies when death is this close...

251
00:30:01,455 --> 00:30:04,995
...Ragatus said it right...

252
00:30:11,235 --> 00:30:12,965
Get the servants ready!

253
00:30:15,745 --> 00:30:19,635
We will go to Kuzgun Hill tomorrow.

254
00:30:22,655 --> 00:30:27,795
I will rip off Osman's liver.

255
00:30:28,795 --> 00:30:30,185
Get out!

256
00:30:38,675 --> 00:30:40,055
I wish it was warmer.

257
00:30:40,115 --> 00:30:42,175
Osman Bey is seen around the tent.

258
00:30:42,245 --> 00:30:44,255
Get him! Quickly!

259
00:30:44,295 --> 00:30:45,595
Let's go!

260
00:31:05,045 --> 00:31:07,435
Osman! That's Osman!
Let's get him!

261
00:31:07,755 --> 00:31:09,465
Get him! Come on!

262
00:31:33,505 --> 00:31:34,885
Soldiers.

263
00:32:36,995 --> 00:32:40,105
What's wrong?
Is it tight my boy?

264
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:48,315
Osman?

265
00:32:49,635 --> 00:32:50,965
Bala!

266
00:32:52,465 --> 00:32:55,215
- Osman?
- Longing is over.

267
00:32:57,255 --> 00:33:00,565
Thank goodness!
Thank goodness!

268
00:33:03,675 --> 00:33:05,175
Praise be!

269
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:08,975
How does he kick like that?

270
00:33:11,505 --> 00:33:13,015
His time is near.

271
00:33:13,095 --> 00:33:14,595
It's near, Osman.

272
00:33:14,845 --> 00:33:17,095
As time get's closer, I get more excited.

273
00:33:20,965 --> 00:33:22,545
Don't you worry!

274
00:33:23,755 --> 00:33:26,105
We'll embrace him
soon if Allah permits.

275
00:33:26,225 --> 00:33:27,805
If Allah permits.

276
00:33:28,805 --> 00:33:30,385
What about...

277
00:33:33,665 --> 00:33:35,215
...you just said, my boy.

278
00:33:36,285 --> 00:33:37,615
These clothes...

279
00:33:40,335 --> 00:33:42,035
...is it a boy.

280
00:33:42,575 --> 00:33:44,075
I feel so.

281
00:33:57,045 --> 00:33:59,215
- My son?
- Mother.

282
00:33:59,835 --> 00:34:01,935
I could not believe it
when I got the word.

283
00:34:01,965 --> 00:34:04,515
Welcome, my dear boy!

284
00:34:05,185 --> 00:34:08,304
Happy to be here, mother!
Happy to be here!

285
00:34:09,225 --> 00:34:10,594
Welcome my bey!

286
00:34:11,603 --> 00:34:12,955
Happy to be here!

287
00:34:14,885 --> 00:34:16,143
How did you come?

288
00:34:16,514 --> 00:34:18,945
I hope Gündüz Bey or
Seljuk soldiers hear this.

289
00:34:21,824 --> 00:34:24,405
My alps removed the alps from the tent.

290
00:34:24,764 --> 00:34:26,313
Do not worry at all.

291
00:34:28,195 --> 00:34:30,245
Gündüz Bey knows I'm here.

292
00:34:31,813 --> 00:34:33,675
What are you saying, son?

293
00:34:33,735 --> 00:34:35,475
How come?

294
00:34:35,725 --> 00:34:38,505
Did Gündüz understand his mistake?

295
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:45,185
It was late but...

296
00:34:45,975 --> 00:34:49,045
...Gündüz Bey's blind eyes
have opened a little bit.

297
00:34:51,715 --> 00:34:53,813
He saw Vizier's treachery.

298
00:34:54,074 --> 00:34:57,955
Thank goodness, he saw the truth!

299
00:35:00,085 --> 00:35:02,855
How could we trust him after
all that he has done, my bey?

300
00:35:03,045 --> 00:35:06,255
Will, we just forget what he
has put us and the tent through?

301
00:35:06,485 --> 00:35:07,995
Of course, we won't.

302
00:35:08,275 --> 00:35:10,315
He'll pay for what he has done.

303
00:35:11,755 --> 00:35:13,805
Justice will be served.

304
00:35:16,525 --> 00:35:19,605
What are you going to do to Gündüz, son?

305
00:35:22,585 --> 00:35:24,845
The end of the traitors is clear, mother.

306
00:35:32,505 --> 00:35:34,515
All this time...

307
00:35:36,015 --> 00:35:37,795
...you did not care for the throne...

308
00:35:40,345 --> 00:35:41,885
...or for the fame.

309
00:35:47,405 --> 00:35:49,915
Now, look at what have
you gotten yourself into?

310
00:35:56,895 --> 00:36:04,015
How will you look at your ancestor's
face on judgment day, Gündüz Bey?

311
00:36:11,835 --> 00:36:13,625
Above all...

312
00:36:14,885 --> 00:36:17,445
...how are you going to
forgive yourself, Gündüz Bey?

313
00:36:19,215 --> 00:36:20,975
May I come in, my bey?

314
00:36:53,385 --> 00:36:54,705
Come in.

315
00:37:00,965 --> 00:37:03,065
Gündüz Bey, beys are coming.

316
00:37:04,395 --> 00:37:05,715
Let them come.

317
00:37:15,125 --> 00:37:19,175
- Selam Alaykum, my bey!
- Selam Alaykum!

318
00:37:21,175 --> 00:37:22,725
Alaykum Selam!

319
00:37:26,675 --> 00:37:28,195
What's wrong, my bey?

320
00:37:28,275 --> 00:37:30,995
What's wrong Gündüz Bey?
What is the rush?

321
00:37:32,595 --> 00:37:33,985
There is nothing wrong.

322
00:37:37,605 --> 00:37:41,405
It is time to leave the
throne to the best.

323
00:37:45,555 --> 00:37:47,065
What is he talking about?

324
00:37:56,515 --> 00:37:57,885
Who is that?

325
00:37:57,885 --> 00:37:59,625
Why is dressed like that?

326
00:38:00,555 --> 00:38:02,115
- Who is that?
- I don't know.

327
00:38:02,205 --> 00:38:03,795
I wonder who that is.

328
00:38:03,815 --> 00:38:05,165
Who could it be?

329
00:38:06,925 --> 00:38:08,665
Osman Bey is here.

330
00:38:08,665 --> 00:38:12,675
- It's Osman Bey!
- It's Osman Bey!

331
00:38:12,675 --> 00:38:14,405
Osman Bey is here!

332
00:38:14,565 --> 00:38:17,835
- Welcome, my bey!
- Welcome!

333
00:38:35,445 --> 00:38:36,995
Servants of my tent...

334
00:38:39,305 --> 00:38:41,085
...excuse me!

335
00:38:43,085 --> 00:38:45,825
I woke from sleep.

336
00:38:50,695 --> 00:38:52,205
Turk's bey...

337
00:38:54,065 --> 00:38:55,575
...Turk's soldier...

338
00:38:56,575 --> 00:38:58,335
...has been famous for his loyalty...

339
00:38:59,235 --> 00:39:01,735
...since Mete Khan.

340
00:39:04,595 --> 00:39:07,095
When his bey says something he does it.

341
00:39:08,005 --> 00:39:10,205
He dies if he says so.

342
00:39:11,815 --> 00:39:14,015
When the head wolf departs...

343
00:39:14,365 --> 00:39:16,465
...he follows him until death!

344
00:39:19,355 --> 00:39:21,435
The thickness of the wolf's neck...

345
00:39:22,885 --> 00:39:25,425
...is because of handling
his own business.

346
00:39:27,345 --> 00:39:30,345
You count what Vizier has
given you as a conquest.

347
00:39:31,345 --> 00:39:35,355
Whoever sits on somebody else's
property, loses their freedom.

348
00:39:39,395 --> 00:39:43,835
Beys! You have not become beys for Kayı...

349
00:39:45,005 --> 00:39:47,095
...but servants for Vizier.

350
00:39:47,675 --> 00:39:51,725
Osman Bey, ask us to kill, we'll
kill, ask us to die, we'll die.

351
00:39:52,095 --> 00:39:54,185
We're only servants for Allah.

352
00:39:54,595 --> 00:40:01,785
The ones who fall into heedlessness, the
ones who commit cruelty should be...

353
00:40:01,865 --> 00:40:06,505
...stopped with your hands if you can't do
that then you warn them with your mouth.

354
00:40:07,025 --> 00:40:13,535
If not then, you will use your heart
to hate them.

355
00:40:17,965 --> 00:40:20,005
If you cannot do that...

356
00:40:22,625 --> 00:40:23,955
...then...

357
00:40:25,875 --> 00:40:27,615
...your humanity finishes.

358
00:40:33,715 --> 00:40:37,785
Some of you would rather die in sleep...

359
00:40:37,975 --> 00:40:41,025
...than to die in battle.

360
00:40:44,125 --> 00:40:49,185
Some of you are sheep in wolfskin.

361
00:40:51,395 --> 00:40:57,895
The ones who obeyed Gündüz Bey will pay.

362
00:41:00,535 --> 00:41:03,655
My bey, we just didn't want
the throne to be vacant.

363
00:41:03,735 --> 00:41:05,285
We're with you.

364
00:41:06,075 --> 00:41:11,805
Sometimes stopping is
better than going off a clip.

365
00:41:20,835 --> 00:41:23,275
If you're with me, you'll
accept your punishment.

366
00:41:27,885 --> 00:41:29,975
You all fell into heedleness.

367
00:41:33,325 --> 00:41:35,365
And you'll pay for that.

368
00:41:43,745 --> 00:41:46,925
- Couldn't you find him, brother?
- We couldn't find him, brother.

369
00:41:51,115 --> 00:41:53,375
I'll tell Gündüz Bey we couldn't find him.

370
00:41:59,465 --> 00:42:01,505
I'll tell Güzndüz Bey, brother.

371
00:42:02,655 --> 00:42:04,725
It is my duty Boran Alp.

372
00:42:09,015 --> 00:42:13,115
Brother, you'll get your bones broken.

373
00:42:18,175 --> 00:42:19,485
Move aside!

374
00:42:21,955 --> 00:42:24,155
Why don't you want
us to get inside the tent?

375
00:42:24,305 --> 00:42:27,815
Or, is Osman Bey in the tent?

376
00:42:39,065 --> 00:42:40,795
Come on, brother!
Come on!

377
00:42:43,435 --> 00:42:45,465
Surrendering is not in our tradition.

378
00:42:47,115 --> 00:42:51,425
Kayı Tent will fight
till its last breathe.

379
00:42:52,325 --> 00:42:56,855
The fire of rebellion will flare up
in the heart of the Turkmen tribes.

380
00:42:57,265 --> 00:42:59,825
We will flare up the fire in these parts.

381
00:43:00,725 --> 00:43:02,475
Excuse us, Osman Bey!

382
00:43:02,795 --> 00:43:06,385
Gündüz Bey did a lot to
save us from this fire.

383
00:43:06,785 --> 00:43:08,965
And you still talk about fire.

384
00:43:09,705 --> 00:43:12,225
We will flare the fire in Kayı.

385
00:43:15,265 --> 00:43:19,825
Anyone who doesn't want
to burn should go, Varul Bey.

386
00:43:20,345 --> 00:43:22,845
Must we burn, Osman Bey?

387
00:43:22,895 --> 00:43:25,395
Can't we live in prosperity as well?

388
00:43:30,255 --> 00:43:32,775
Everyone wants to be rich.

389
00:43:37,975 --> 00:43:40,115
Anybody who wants to lose their freedom...

390
00:43:42,115 --> 00:43:44,205
...can go spend someone else's money.

391
00:43:48,005 --> 00:43:49,395
Now,...

392
00:43:53,005 --> 00:43:57,625
...take your kid and hatun
and get out of here.

393
00:43:58,485 --> 00:44:00,815
Go somewhere you'll be rich.

394
00:44:05,675 --> 00:44:11,595
The one who has a love for money
in their heart instead of courage...

395
00:44:13,425 --> 00:44:14,945
...is not one of us.

396
00:44:16,605 --> 00:44:18,635
- What are you...
- Get out!

397
00:44:39,235 --> 00:44:45,285
Anyone whose heart hadn't darkened when
the Turk is oppressed, can stay with us.

398
00:44:50,405 --> 00:44:52,455
If anyone has something to say, say it.

399
00:44:52,655 --> 00:44:55,865
My bey, you say courage,
and may Allah bless you!

400
00:44:56,165 --> 00:44:58,545
But you are allied with Nikola...

401
00:44:59,035 --> 00:45:01,665
...they killed a lot of our valiants.

402
00:45:02,865 --> 00:45:04,905
Don't worry at all.

403
00:45:06,295 --> 00:45:08,325
After we defeat Geyhatu...

404
00:45:08,855 --> 00:45:12,615
...we'll make Nikola pay for
all the blood he has shed.

405
00:45:13,275 --> 00:45:15,375
My bey, Nikola knows this as well.

406
00:45:15,595 --> 00:45:18,405
He won't wait for Geyhatu
to go to stab us in the back.

407
00:45:19,455 --> 00:45:21,215
Have no worry.

408
00:45:22,025 --> 00:45:26,585
Emperor Andronikos
gave me Nikola's bridles.

409
00:45:27,815 --> 00:45:33,205
He can't do anything to us.

410
00:45:37,705 --> 00:45:39,725
If anyone has doubt...

411
00:45:40,975 --> 00:45:43,505
...they can follow Varul Bey.

412
00:45:49,595 --> 00:45:51,325
There is no turning back.

413
00:45:53,175 --> 00:45:57,695
Government comes before all!

414
00:45:59,205 --> 00:46:03,295
Mother is it true that
Osman Bey has come?

415
00:46:04,115 --> 00:46:06,175
Is he with Gündüz?

416
00:46:14,815 --> 00:46:17,755
Mother, may Allah protect him...

417
00:46:17,895 --> 00:46:20,485
...will he do something to Gündüz?

418
00:46:20,595 --> 00:46:22,885
It's where words fail my girl.

419
00:46:27,065 --> 00:46:29,075
It's up to Osman Bey.

420
00:46:34,235 --> 00:46:36,295
What can I say Ayşe?

421
00:46:36,335 --> 00:46:40,335
When you took care of my Orhan,
he separated me from my child.

422
00:46:44,665 --> 00:46:47,565
It's not time to speak out.
Let's hope for the best for him.

423
00:47:13,645 --> 00:47:15,655
What did Geyhatu say?

424
00:47:16,935 --> 00:47:19,525
He asked about the alps I promised him.

425
00:47:21,595 --> 00:47:23,845
And I told them that
they're all at the tent.

426
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:30,095
Did he just ask that?

427
00:47:32,285 --> 00:47:33,815
He asked about you as well.

428
00:47:36,025 --> 00:47:39,815
I told him that I didn't know where
you were and that I was after you.

429
00:47:41,385 --> 00:47:42,765
He did not suspect anything.

430
00:47:44,415 --> 00:47:46,615
He won't.

431
00:47:48,095 --> 00:47:50,175
You got covered in mud with the traitor.

432
00:47:51,905 --> 00:47:54,255
You ate with the traitor.

433
00:47:59,725 --> 00:48:01,645
Of course, he'll not suspect anything.

434
00:48:02,855 --> 00:48:09,155
Whatever you say, you are right, brother.

435
00:48:11,545 --> 00:48:13,685
But I was never cruel like them.

436
00:48:16,375 --> 00:48:18,405
I just got tricked by them.

437
00:48:18,935 --> 00:48:25,745
There is no difference between the cruel
and the one who follows him, brother.

438
00:48:29,225 --> 00:48:31,315
You talked about salvation before...

439
00:48:35,485 --> 00:48:38,055
...now you talk about getting tricked.

440
00:48:40,255 --> 00:48:42,535
Don't get tricked brother.

441
00:48:43,655 --> 00:48:48,795
Don't believe their words, brother.

442
00:48:53,375 --> 00:48:55,625
A Muslim must be awake.

443
00:48:55,945 --> 00:48:59,215
A Muslim must know to learn his lesson.

444
00:49:01,145 --> 00:49:03,735
You did not draw a lesson from uncle?

445
00:49:05,965 --> 00:49:08,475
Tell me.

446
00:49:09,945 --> 00:49:12,505
You did not draw a lesson from him.

447
00:49:13,335 --> 00:49:15,555
You got tricked by them and...

448
00:49:17,375 --> 00:49:23,655
...made yourself and
the tent their servant.

449
00:49:26,125 --> 00:49:28,135
Heedlessness is haram to us.

450
00:49:31,375 --> 00:49:34,535
The punishment of the ones who
fall into heedlessness is clear.

451
00:49:58,025 --> 00:49:59,555
It is clear.

452
00:50:01,715 --> 00:50:11,305
For that reason, my blood is
halal for you, brother.

453
00:50:46,805 --> 00:50:49,435
I believe that you are awaken now.

454
00:50:54,695 --> 00:51:01,455
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son, Gündüz Bey.

455
00:51:05,755 --> 00:51:08,695
Your pardon is not at me anymore.

456
00:51:10,855 --> 00:51:12,975
I spare your life, brother.

457
00:51:15,635 --> 00:51:17,015
But...

458
00:51:19,155 --> 00:51:34,495
but your treason to our brotherhood,
our laws and customs won't be forgotten.

459
00:51:37,995 --> 00:51:53,035
As long as this body carries this head,
I won't forget nor forgive what I did.

460
00:51:58,655 --> 00:52:00,405
If you do...

461
00:52:04,095 --> 00:52:06,335
don't return to the tribe, brother.

462
00:52:18,655 --> 00:52:20,035
Boran.

463
00:52:24,755 --> 00:52:25,815
Yes, my bey.

464
00:52:26,215 --> 00:52:29,705
Tell the ladies.
They should lay a table.

465
00:52:30,505 --> 00:52:32,015
As you order, my bey.

466
00:52:40,725 --> 00:52:43,755
Söğüt

467
00:52:57,335 --> 00:52:58,865
Salam Alaikum.

468
00:52:59,415 --> 00:53:00,975
Alaikum Salam.

469
00:53:13,835 --> 00:53:16,425
I was expecting you, Güngör Bey.

470
00:53:17,255 --> 00:53:21,765
Karamanoğulları are revolting.
Things are getting complicated.

471
00:53:22,615 --> 00:53:26,965
Emperor Androkinos gathered
his commanders.

472
00:53:27,335 --> 00:53:31,375
Everyone is taking a position.

473
00:53:34,495 --> 00:53:37,025
What's the cause of this chaos?

474
00:53:37,365 --> 00:53:41,375
It's Geyhatu who I sharpen
my blade behind.

475
00:53:42,235 --> 00:53:46,345
All his shields are raised against
his enemies, Güngör Bey.

476
00:53:47,275 --> 00:53:51,875
I'm his enemy in disguise.

477
00:53:52,585 --> 00:53:54,395
Why are you waiting for this long?

478
00:53:54,575 --> 00:53:57,215
Why is Geyhatu still alive, Alemşah?

479
00:53:58,265 --> 00:54:03,405
Geyhatu is the greatest trouble
in these lands.

480
00:54:04,995 --> 00:54:08,905
The one who saves the lands from the
trouble becomes the owner of them.

481
00:54:09,695 --> 00:54:12,545
The one who kills Geyhatu becomes
the sultan.

482
00:54:13,075 --> 00:54:17,965
I think that my bey should do such
a sacred thing.

483
00:54:21,175 --> 00:54:22,475
Good.

484
00:54:26,035 --> 00:54:28,325
I have my brother's seal.

485
00:54:28,495 --> 00:54:32,995
So, it's my duty to destroy
Geyhatu.

486
00:54:34,035 --> 00:54:38,255
I'll make a throne out of Geyhatu's
bones for my brother.

487
00:54:40,515 --> 00:54:50,045
Once the borders are saved from Geyhatu,
everyone will be loyal to my bey.

488
00:54:50,855 --> 00:54:53,385
While I'm digging a grave for
Geyhatu...

489
00:54:53,555 --> 00:54:57,145
you'll have another job, Alemşah.

490
00:55:06,465 --> 00:55:09,735
My Orhan...
My Orhan...

491
00:55:13,515 --> 00:55:18,275
Mashallah to my lion!

492
00:55:31,045 --> 00:55:32,585
Come on.

493
00:55:39,705 --> 00:55:43,225
Light follows a dark night, son.

494
00:55:43,715 --> 00:55:45,495
Thank Allah, mother.

495
00:55:45,895 --> 00:55:47,915
Thank Allah, we are united again.

496
00:55:49,455 --> 00:55:52,015
We haven't laid such a table for
so long, my bey.

497
00:55:52,095 --> 00:55:53,625
We missed it.

498
00:55:53,655 --> 00:55:56,665
True. We missed it.

499
00:55:58,295 --> 00:56:05,395
But you acted my bravely than
men.

500
00:56:06,375 --> 00:56:07,635
Thank you.

501
00:56:12,835 --> 00:56:14,145
Thank you.

502
00:56:20,055 --> 00:56:22,225
It'll be harder from now on.

503
00:56:22,535 --> 00:56:35,275
If we stay united, we can overcome
them all.

504
00:56:36,615 --> 00:56:40,205
As long as we have you,
we can overcome anything.

505
00:56:40,265 --> 00:56:41,835
Thank you.

506
00:56:41,905 --> 00:56:43,295
Thank you.

507
00:56:45,135 --> 00:56:48,195
It's not the first time I'm separated
from my family.

508
00:56:49,775 --> 00:56:51,165
But...

509
00:56:55,335 --> 00:56:57,765
this was a lot harder.

510
00:57:04,715 --> 00:57:09,075
I wouldn't have worries back
then...

511
00:57:10,095 --> 00:57:13,435
I would trust that my brother
would protect my loved ones.

512
00:57:19,685 --> 00:57:21,255
Brother.

513
00:57:23,535 --> 00:57:31,085
Ask for forgiveness from the ones you
hurt and bled.

514
00:58:06,135 --> 00:58:08,145
I trusted the tongue of the devil...

515
00:58:10,165 --> 00:58:13,235
what I've done keeps burning
my heart.

516
00:58:14,245 --> 00:58:19,825
In this short time, I made you suffer
a lot.

517
00:58:24,415 --> 00:58:26,765
I can't look at any of you.

518
00:58:28,935 --> 00:58:35,435
All I can do is ask for forgiveness.

519
00:58:43,075 --> 00:58:44,445
Mother.

520
00:58:52,115 --> 00:58:53,615
Mother, you too.

521
00:58:59,945 --> 00:59:01,255
Give me your blessing.

522
00:59:12,685 --> 00:59:17,255
It is never too late to repent.

523
00:59:37,695 --> 00:59:43,155
Now, your duty is harder.
It's time to rebuild.

524
00:59:46,425 --> 00:59:51,105
If Orhan was hurt, then you wouldn't
be forgiven.

525
00:59:55,695 --> 00:59:57,695
You have my blessing, Gündüz Bey.

526
01:00:01,235 --> 01:00:06,475
If one of us were hurt, Gündüz Bey...
But, like our mother says...

527
01:00:07,445 --> 01:00:10,665
thank Allah, we are safe and sound.

528
01:00:11,965 --> 01:00:13,755
You have my blessing.

529
01:00:26,290 --> 01:00:28,340
Thank Allah, my mother is well.

530
01:00:29,210 --> 01:00:30,990
You have my blessing.

531
01:00:33,410 --> 01:00:35,430
Thank Allah, Gündüz Bey.

532
01:00:36,410 --> 01:00:37,920
Thank Allah.

533
01:01:26,860 --> 01:01:28,950
Enjoy your meals now.

534
01:01:29,600 --> 01:01:32,170
With the name of Allah.

535
01:01:47,550 --> 01:01:50,150
Osman the dark doesn't know
his limits.

536
01:01:51,110 --> 01:01:55,850
Now, he informs the beys about
gathering a council.

537
01:01:57,290 --> 01:01:59,390
I'm the ruler of these borders.

538
01:02:00,310 --> 01:02:03,350
The beys are using my gold...

539
01:02:03,770 --> 01:02:06,510
and they are going to Osman's
council.

540
01:02:07,370 --> 01:02:08,870
Look at this!

541
01:02:09,830 --> 01:02:11,530
I'm speaking my bey's information.

542
01:02:12,590 --> 01:02:15,290
This is your job, Alemşah.

543
01:02:16,070 --> 01:02:19,150
As long as I have his tribe even...

544
01:02:19,150 --> 01:02:22,650
the council he'll form won't
pose any threat.

545
01:02:23,390 --> 01:02:28,470
I hold the wires of his brother
who sits on the throne.

546
01:02:29,430 --> 01:02:36,750
But it's my responsibility to behead
Osman and those beys.

547
01:02:38,230 --> 01:02:41,790
I'll destroy Geyhatu and you'll
destroy the revolting beys.

548
01:02:42,870 --> 01:02:46,710
There should be no obstacle in my
brother's way to sultanate.

549
01:02:50,630 --> 01:02:53,130
How do you plan to kill Geyhatu?

550
01:02:54,750 --> 01:02:57,270
Did my bey send an army?

551
01:02:59,250 --> 01:03:01,770
No. I will do it personally.

552
01:03:04,510 --> 01:03:07,050
An army protects Geyhatu.

553
01:03:07,330 --> 01:03:08,850
How will you do it?

554
01:03:10,410 --> 01:03:12,810
With mind, Alemşah.
With mind.

555
01:03:12,810 --> 01:03:17,530
Mind is a greater weapon than all
the armies combined.

556
01:03:19,770 --> 01:03:22,150
I'll hit Geyhatu from where
he doesn't expect it.

557
01:03:24,850 --> 01:03:28,410
Osman is also looking for away to
kill Geyhatu.

558
01:03:30,130 --> 01:03:31,710
Be quick.

559
01:03:38,430 --> 01:03:39,770
Alright.

560
01:03:55,090 --> 01:03:56,590
Soldier!

561
01:04:00,590 --> 01:04:02,170
Summon Konur.

562
01:04:06,410 --> 01:04:07,950
Cerkutay.

563
01:04:08,850 --> 01:04:10,230
My bey.

564
01:04:12,550 --> 01:04:13,870
Mother.

565
01:04:19,090 --> 01:04:20,650
With Allah's order...

566
01:04:23,770 --> 01:04:30,890
and our prophet's wish,
peace be upon him...

567
01:04:33,670 --> 01:04:35,130
I ask for my sister Aygül...

568
01:04:39,350 --> 01:04:42,690
to my brave Cerkutay.

569
01:04:59,970 --> 01:05:05,950
Cerkutay, tell me.
Will you take good care of my daughter?

570
01:05:14,290 --> 01:05:16,050
I will, mother.

571
01:05:17,230 --> 01:05:18,970
Then, you have my permission.

572
01:05:26,910 --> 01:05:28,210
But...

573
01:05:29,470 --> 01:05:32,050
there is no point in waiting.

574
01:05:35,190 --> 01:05:37,770
Ladies, prepare...

575
01:05:38,490 --> 01:05:39,990
we'll have a wedding tomorrow.

576
01:05:40,110 --> 01:05:42,230
Let's do it.

577
01:05:49,370 --> 01:05:50,710
My bey.

578
01:05:52,950 --> 01:05:54,670
Am I allowed to?

579
01:05:59,110 --> 01:06:00,470
It's yours.

580
01:06:04,010 --> 01:06:06,650
Allah Allah!

581
01:06:06,650 --> 01:06:09,950
Allah!

582
01:06:09,950 --> 01:06:14,130
Allah Allah!

583
01:06:15,130 --> 01:06:16,870
Stop, you mad man!

584
01:06:16,870 --> 01:06:18,450
Cerkutay.

585
01:06:18,490 --> 01:06:21,450
Allah!

586
01:06:22,370 --> 01:06:24,070
Control yourself.

587
01:06:24,730 --> 01:06:26,470
There are soldiers outside.

588
01:06:45,710 --> 01:06:47,170
Did it fit, brother?

589
01:06:48,890 --> 01:06:50,670
Mashallah, brother.

590
01:06:58,690 --> 01:07:00,250
Brothers!

591
01:07:00,610 --> 01:07:02,310
In the evening...

592
01:07:02,390 --> 01:07:04,910
no one should be hungry at my
wedding.

593
01:07:05,230 --> 01:07:06,990
Don't worry, brother.

594
01:07:07,470 --> 01:07:08,810
But...

595
01:07:10,950 --> 01:07:12,770
let's make sure
you are fed...

596
01:07:13,190 --> 01:07:14,830
the rest is easy.

597
01:07:20,850 --> 01:07:29,370
No, no, no, no.
No, no, no, no.

598
01:07:35,650 --> 01:07:37,030
Come on.

599
01:07:37,050 --> 01:07:38,750
Allow me, brother.

600
01:07:48,350 --> 01:07:50,110
What are you looking at?
Come on.

601
01:07:55,910 --> 01:07:57,250
Kumral Abdal!

602
01:07:57,310 --> 01:07:59,330
This way!

603
01:08:09,450 --> 01:08:11,510
This is the end of our friendship.

604
01:08:12,890 --> 01:08:16,010
But we are separating for a
holy cause.

605
01:08:22,350 --> 01:08:23,930
I'm not sad.

606
01:08:24,010 --> 01:08:25,550
Why should I be?

607
01:08:25,850 --> 01:08:28,390
You will be a food for two lovers'
wedding!

608
01:08:29,430 --> 01:08:31,448
Is there a better fate?

609
01:08:31,850 --> 01:08:33,189
There can't be.

610
01:08:35,868 --> 01:08:37,630
It'll be sacrificed for love.

611
01:08:40,229 --> 01:08:41,729
Mashallah!

612
01:08:42,328 --> 01:08:43,710
Come on.

613
01:08:43,729 --> 01:08:45,810
With the name of Allah.

614
01:08:50,948 --> 01:08:52,290
Brothers!

615
01:08:52,970 --> 01:08:55,109
I don't want any problem at my wedding!

616
01:09:00,970 --> 01:09:04,029
All power to your elbows, brothers!

617
01:09:05,470 --> 01:09:07,210
Brother, how does it taste?

618
01:09:07,210 --> 01:09:08,710
It's good.

619
01:09:08,710 --> 01:09:10,710
It's rich in meat, right?

620
01:09:16,448 --> 01:09:19,310
It's rich in meat as long as
you don't eat them, brother.

621
01:09:19,310 --> 01:09:20,630
I won't.

622
01:09:25,790 --> 01:09:30,908
Allahu Aqbar.
Allahu Aqbar.

623
01:09:31,250 --> 01:09:36,430
There is no god but Allah.

624
01:09:36,430 --> 01:09:41,470
Allahu Aqbar.

625
01:09:41,590 --> 01:09:43,090
Cerkutay, stop.

626
01:09:43,130 --> 01:09:44,670
You'll eat it all!

627
01:09:44,670 --> 01:09:46,670
I'm still hungry, brother!

628
01:09:47,189 --> 01:09:48,750
I eat but I'm still hungry!

629
01:09:52,050 --> 01:09:54,210
It's excitement, Cerkutay.

630
01:09:54,210 --> 01:09:56,910
It's excitement, Akça Dervish.

631
01:09:57,890 --> 01:09:59,410
Stop, Cerkutay.

632
01:09:59,510 --> 01:10:03,990
Brother Boran, take him away or there
will be no food left.

633
01:10:05,290 --> 01:10:07,870
Cerkutay, come, brother.

634
01:10:09,470 --> 01:10:11,030
Look, brother.

635
01:10:13,470 --> 01:10:15,470
The secret of love is patience.

636
01:10:15,470 --> 01:10:17,470
The end of patience is peace.

637
01:10:19,530 --> 01:10:21,030
May Allah give you happiness.

638
01:10:21,290 --> 01:10:24,670
Amin, Kumral Abdal.
Amin!

639
01:10:24,950 --> 01:10:26,790
Amin!

640
01:10:31,490 --> 01:10:33,110
What is this excitement, brother?

641
01:10:33,110 --> 01:10:35,350
We are excited, brother!

642
01:10:37,950 --> 01:10:39,670
Leave my brother alone.

643
01:10:39,830 --> 01:10:42,910
He waited a lot.
He is excited.

644
01:10:42,950 --> 01:10:44,670
Let them have their fun!

645
01:10:44,670 --> 01:10:46,030
Let them!

646
01:10:46,130 --> 01:10:47,910
I'm with my Aygül!

647
01:10:47,910 --> 01:10:50,470
Let them have as much as
fun as they want!

648
01:10:54,270 --> 01:10:56,350
Let me eat a little more.

649
01:10:56,450 --> 01:10:59,030
Cerkutay, let's go.

650
01:10:59,030 --> 01:11:01,290
Let's go.

651
01:11:03,590 --> 01:11:04,910
Come on.

652
01:12:02,750 --> 01:12:07,070
Before you, I would come here
with Karayel.

653
01:12:12,950 --> 01:12:14,690
Now, you are my companion.

654
01:12:18,470 --> 01:12:19,610
These lands...

655
01:12:22,150 --> 01:12:27,490
will be a part of the country we'll
form for order.

656
01:12:29,290 --> 01:12:30,630
But...

657
01:12:32,790 --> 01:12:35,430
but not only the lands
that my eyes can see...

658
01:12:37,410 --> 01:12:44,670
beyond the plains and mountains too!

659
01:12:49,650 --> 01:12:56,610
I'll spread Allah's 99 names to all
over the world!

660
01:12:59,250 --> 01:13:01,350
My Allah...

661
01:13:03,830 --> 01:13:05,890
my Allah!

662
01:13:53,370 --> 01:13:54,750
Who are you?

663
01:13:54,750 --> 01:13:56,250
What do you want?

664
01:13:56,370 --> 01:13:58,150
Move out of my way!

665
01:13:58,490 --> 01:14:00,250
I don't seek evil, merchant.

666
01:14:00,310 --> 01:14:02,090
I want to trade.

667
01:14:02,430 --> 01:14:04,210
What are you carrying?

668
01:14:04,290 --> 01:14:06,510
My goods aren't for sale.

669
01:14:06,510 --> 01:14:10,090
Every merchant sells their goods
if the price is good.

670
01:14:11,030 --> 01:14:13,570
If I owned the goods,
of course.

671
01:14:13,930 --> 01:14:15,990
But I don't own them.

672
01:14:16,830 --> 01:14:18,590
It's Geyhatu.

673
01:14:19,250 --> 01:14:21,630
It won't do you good to meddle.

674
01:14:22,210 --> 01:14:23,930
Not only your goods...

675
01:14:24,350 --> 01:14:29,210
I want you, your animals
and these men.

676
01:14:30,830 --> 01:14:32,850
I'll pay ten times the price.

677
01:14:45,530 --> 01:14:47,870
We'll carry the goods together, merchant.

678
01:14:48,230 --> 01:14:50,290
And I'll give you a thousand coins.

679
01:14:51,410 --> 01:14:53,470
You'll take me into the quarters.

680
01:14:54,270 --> 01:14:56,290
You'll have a thousand coins.

681
01:14:59,470 --> 01:15:01,670
And you'll keep yourself alive, merchant.

682
01:15:14,150 --> 01:15:15,710
There will be blood!

683
01:15:20,230 --> 01:15:22,190
There will be a lot of blood!

684
01:15:25,210 --> 01:15:27,340
Hell will come down to this world!

685
01:15:35,150 --> 01:15:38,930
There is blood on great Geyhatu!

686
01:15:38,930 --> 01:15:40,930
It's Osman's blood!

687
01:15:41,090 --> 01:15:42,430
Tell me!

688
01:15:42,430 --> 01:15:44,930
The blood of those who revolt
to Geyhatu.

689
01:15:45,110 --> 01:15:46,590
Tell me about the skulls!

690
01:15:46,810 --> 01:15:49,110
Tell me about the beheaded!

691
01:15:56,390 --> 01:15:59,210
There are no heads over
the shoulders.

692
01:15:59,210 --> 01:16:01,210
Geyhatu will win this war.

693
01:16:02,470 --> 01:16:06,450
He'll control these lands.

694
01:16:06,450 --> 01:16:10,050
Tell me! Is it just
these lands?

695
01:16:24,730 --> 01:16:29,390
Spreading, just like blood...

696
01:16:32,030 --> 01:16:38,050
Geyhatu's rule spreads into
the whole world!

697
01:17:08,250 --> 01:17:10,930
First, these lands...

698
01:17:18,150 --> 01:17:23,010
then, Argun Khan's throne...

699
01:17:26,490 --> 01:17:31,650
then, the whole world!

700
01:17:32,330 --> 01:17:34,710
The whole world!

701
01:17:35,470 --> 01:17:39,510
The whole world!

702
01:17:39,510 --> 01:17:41,820
We've been fighting for
a long time, Kosses.

703
01:17:43,130 --> 01:17:44,490
Are you tired?

704
01:17:45,070 --> 01:17:46,430
Never.

705
01:17:46,690 --> 01:17:51,830
The men of our dynasty had fought
and died on the battlefield for centuries.

706
01:17:52,790 --> 01:17:54,610
We don't get tired of war, Osman Bey.

707
01:17:55,190 --> 01:17:56,530
On the contrary...

708
01:17:56,610 --> 01:18:00,890
being close to death makes
me feel alive.

709
01:18:01,850 --> 01:18:03,930
Death is always upon us.

710
01:18:05,610 --> 01:18:07,390
Have you...

711
01:18:09,110 --> 01:18:10,850
missed your castle?

712
01:18:16,770 --> 01:18:22,110
I missed my castle as much as
you missed your throne.

713
01:18:24,190 --> 01:18:25,750
It's time.

714
01:18:27,510 --> 01:18:29,270
You can go to your throne.

715
01:18:31,150 --> 01:18:33,370
Harmankaya Castle belongs to you.

716
01:18:35,470 --> 01:18:37,250
Thank you for your help.

717
01:18:38,890 --> 01:18:43,150
So, we are at the end of
this adventure.

718
01:18:44,290 --> 01:18:46,330
Our unity was until getting
the castle.

719
01:18:49,850 --> 01:18:51,910
Time will show that.

720
01:18:57,010 --> 01:18:58,310
What about...

721
01:19:00,470 --> 01:19:02,470
Gündüz Bey?

722
01:19:04,850 --> 01:19:06,910
What is he saying
about that?

723
01:19:09,430 --> 01:19:11,450
He'll visit you at the castle.

724
01:19:13,510 --> 01:19:15,230
You can ask him yourself.

725
01:19:18,650 --> 01:19:20,370
I see, Osman.

726
01:19:26,630 --> 01:19:28,910
I'm grateful for everything.

727
01:19:32,110 --> 01:19:34,510
If you want to feel that
you are alive...

728
01:19:36,130 --> 01:19:38,750
we can fight shoulder to shoulder
again.

729
01:19:43,390 --> 01:19:46,130
Thank you, Osman Bey.

730
01:19:51,570 --> 01:19:52,910
Thank you.

731
01:20:13,410 --> 01:20:16,470
These are Geyhatu's provisions.

732
01:20:30,930 --> 01:20:32,270
Go.

733
01:21:03,655 --> 01:21:05,355
Why are you late?

734
01:21:10,115 --> 01:21:11,455
Answer me!

735
01:21:11,895 --> 01:21:14,675
Bandits attacked us on the road.

736
01:21:20,375 --> 01:21:22,075
Why didn't they kill you?

737
01:21:22,415 --> 01:21:24,855
We told them the provisions
were Geyhatu's.

738
01:21:25,082 --> 01:21:27,538
No one walks to their death.

739
01:21:44,175 --> 01:21:45,515
Stop!

740
01:21:48,555 --> 01:21:50,055
There are there!

741
01:22:07,645 --> 01:22:10,955
Rebellion to the State of Seljuk means
death.

742
01:22:12,725 --> 01:22:16,295
Osman is a traitor who even tried to kill
the Sultan.

743
01:22:17,135 --> 01:22:22,895
You will kill him and those who help him.
For the State of Seljuk.

744
01:22:25,355 --> 01:22:26,735
Vizier...

745
01:22:26,835 --> 01:22:30,135
...everyone we will ambush is Turkmens.
Are you sure?

746
01:22:31,135 --> 01:22:36,525
When did your duty become questioning
your master, Konur?

747
01:22:37,445 --> 01:22:40,835
Those who seem loyal to me but work with
Osman are traitors.

748
01:22:41,335 --> 01:22:43,925
The traitor cannot be separated as
Turkmen or Bey.

749
01:22:47,365 --> 01:22:49,415
Don't leave a single one alive!

750
01:22:50,745 --> 01:22:52,795
I am coming for you, Osman!

751
01:22:55,205 --> 01:22:57,225
Do you remember, Osman Bey?

752
01:23:00,555 --> 01:23:02,595
You told me something.

753
01:23:04,405 --> 01:23:06,495
You said, no matter how you perceive us...

754
01:23:07,475 --> 01:23:09,525
...we perceive you as one of us.

755
01:23:13,245 --> 01:23:15,285
How did you know I was one of you?

756
01:23:17,475 --> 01:23:19,255
From the way you ride your horse.

757
01:23:23,835 --> 01:23:26,465
Does anyone who is not one of us
ride a horse like this?

758
01:23:27,045 --> 01:23:28,415
Thank you.

759
01:23:31,605 --> 01:23:33,355
You must know that...

760
01:23:33,375 --> 01:23:37,625
...since the day I am one of you, I have
lived in peace.

761
01:23:39,105 --> 01:23:40,475
Thank you.

762
01:23:42,245 --> 01:23:43,625
My Bey!

763
01:23:57,205 --> 01:23:58,785
Osman!

764
01:24:04,005 --> 01:24:06,975
Ambush!
Ambush!

765
01:24:22,135 --> 01:24:23,575
Are you all right, my Vizier?

766
01:24:24,475 --> 01:24:25,985
How did this happen, Konur?

767
01:24:27,695 --> 01:24:29,735
Search everywhere!

768
01:24:33,685 --> 01:24:35,425
It obviously was an ambush.

769
01:24:35,605 --> 01:24:37,655
Let's get you out of the woods first.

770
01:24:38,205 --> 01:24:40,265
There may be another trap.

771
01:24:40,985 --> 01:24:43,785
Osman will pay for this.

772
01:24:47,855 --> 01:24:49,725
And thank you, Konur.

773
01:24:50,225 --> 01:24:52,055
My duty is to protect you, my Vizier.

774
01:24:56,555 --> 01:25:01,845
Osman, how do you know about,
my every move?

775
01:25:09,115 --> 01:25:12,745
Vizier Alemşah found out about where you
will have an assembly with the Beys.

776
01:25:12,785 --> 01:25:14,415
He plans an ambush in the morning.

777
01:25:15,015 --> 01:25:17,335
No other but the Beys knew
about the assembly.

778
01:25:18,455 --> 01:25:20,585
Then there must be a traitor
among the Beys.

779
01:25:21,225 --> 01:25:24,775
My Bey, I give you this information but
the Vizier's suspicions...

780
01:25:25,725 --> 01:25:27,395
...are increasing each day.

781
01:25:28,375 --> 01:25:29,965
We fail every move of him.

782
01:25:31,035 --> 01:25:33,505
First, we will dispel the doubt of
the Vizier.

783
01:25:35,385 --> 01:25:37,685
Then, you will find that traitor.

784
01:25:40,655 --> 01:25:41,835
I will set the trap.

785
01:25:42,595 --> 01:25:44,325
You will save the Vizier.

786
01:25:45,395 --> 01:25:47,135
We can lure him to the trap but...

787
01:25:48,675 --> 01:25:50,755
why aren't we killing him, Osman Bey?

788
01:25:51,745 --> 01:25:53,565
I told you in the beginning.

789
01:25:55,075 --> 01:25:57,085
Information is everything.

790
01:25:58,075 --> 01:25:59,785
Vizier won't die.

791
01:26:00,785 --> 01:26:02,575
He is a familiar enemy.

792
01:26:03,595 --> 01:26:05,105
You are with him.

793
01:26:05,255 --> 01:26:07,335
We know about his every move.

794
01:26:08,145 --> 01:26:09,535
Now...

795
01:26:10,705 --> 01:26:13,235
...now we will finish Geyhatu.

796
01:26:16,425 --> 01:26:17,985
As you order, my Bey.

797
01:26:23,305 --> 01:26:27,005
Soldiers, bring the horses.
We are returning to Söğüt.

798
01:26:35,725 --> 01:26:37,315
Osman...

799
01:26:38,335 --> 01:26:41,835
...you are only raising your suffering.

800
01:26:42,605 --> 01:26:48,075
I will hang you and those rebellious beys
at the entry of Söğüt.

801
01:26:50,775 --> 01:26:53,835
Mashallah to my girl!
You look so beautiful.

802
01:26:58,135 --> 01:27:01,345
Thanks to Allah I could see these days.

803
01:27:01,565 --> 01:27:02,915
Mother...

804
01:27:03,645 --> 01:27:08,145
...you never let me feel the absence of
my parents.

805
01:27:09,785 --> 01:27:12,315
You brought me out of the darkness.

806
01:27:13,135 --> 01:27:14,695
You lightened my way.

807
01:27:15,205 --> 01:27:16,975
How can I ever repay you?

808
01:27:18,275 --> 01:27:20,555
You can repay me by being happy.

809
01:27:23,905 --> 01:27:26,175
Come on, enough of talking.

810
01:27:26,265 --> 01:27:27,565
Come on!

811
01:27:27,565 --> 01:27:29,735
Bring her veil.

812
01:27:30,245 --> 01:27:31,985
Here, Selcen Mother.

813
01:27:32,795 --> 01:27:34,505
Let's put it on.

814
01:27:42,255 --> 01:27:43,815
Praise be!

815
01:27:43,945 --> 01:27:45,245
Come here.

816
01:27:45,935 --> 01:27:47,705
In the name of Allah.

817
01:27:51,495 --> 01:27:53,865
Can we come in, Selcen Mother?

818
01:27:55,725 --> 01:27:57,755
Wait, girl. Don't get excited.

819
01:27:59,505 --> 01:28:01,285
Come in, Cerkutay.

820
01:28:09,005 --> 01:28:11,095
What is that in your hand, son?

821
01:28:12,945 --> 01:28:14,445
Cerkutay?

822
01:28:15,165 --> 01:28:17,785
Cerkutay!
What is that in your hand, son?

823
01:28:19,215 --> 01:28:20,525
Honey.

824
01:28:23,335 --> 01:28:25,035
For what?

825
01:28:34,585 --> 01:28:36,145
Mother...

826
01:28:36,435 --> 01:28:39,105
...you said for sweet talking you need
honey...

827
01:28:39,855 --> 01:28:42,675
...when you were preparing Mari Hatun's
dowry.

828
01:28:43,675 --> 01:28:46,235
This crazy girl needs much of it.

829
01:28:46,265 --> 01:28:48,265
Thus, I brought honey.

830
01:28:48,385 --> 01:28:50,165
You did well, son.

831
01:28:50,415 --> 01:28:53,465
Mashallah to my valiant!

832
01:28:58,775 --> 01:29:02,165
-For sweet talking!
-Amen!

833
01:29:05,295 --> 01:29:06,685
Here you go.

834
01:29:06,705 --> 01:29:08,755
Mother, give her more.

835
01:29:08,755 --> 01:29:10,265
We did, son!

836
01:29:12,785 --> 01:29:15,345
What do we need for intelligence, mother?

837
01:29:15,365 --> 01:29:16,705
Let's feed him that.

838
01:29:16,705 --> 01:29:17,835
Girl!

839
01:29:17,885 --> 01:29:20,435
Look, mother!
It wasn't enough.

840
01:29:20,465 --> 01:29:23,015
You feed her this.
I'll go find a hive.

841
01:29:23,015 --> 01:29:24,405
Don't, son!

842
01:29:24,405 --> 01:29:26,685
Now I will make you eat!

843
01:29:26,685 --> 01:29:28,075
Mother!

844
01:29:28,075 --> 01:29:30,585
Get out before I change my mind, Cerkutay!

845
01:29:31,125 --> 01:29:32,485
Come on!
Come on!

846
01:29:32,545 --> 01:29:33,915
Get out!

847
01:29:34,305 --> 01:29:36,025
Come on, get out!

848
01:29:36,335 --> 01:29:38,845
I don't need sweet talking.

849
01:29:40,935 --> 01:29:42,955
I love you like this.

850
01:29:46,285 --> 01:29:47,795
-Son, get out!
-Mother.

851
01:29:47,795 --> 01:29:49,795
Come on!
Come on!

852
01:30:03,365 --> 01:30:05,245
Aygül, daughter of Dündar...

853
01:30:06,605 --> 01:30:09,115
...do you take son of Cengiz, Cerkutay...

854
01:30:09,805 --> 01:30:17,195
...as your husband by giving you a hundred
dirhams of gold and ten sheep as gifts?

855
01:30:22,125 --> 01:30:23,455
I do.

856
01:30:26,045 --> 01:30:28,195
-Do you?
-I do.

857
01:30:28,615 --> 01:30:30,695
-Do you?
-I do.

858
01:30:33,295 --> 01:30:35,495
Son of Cengiz, Cerkutay...

859
01:30:36,575 --> 01:30:38,335
...do you take...

860
01:30:38,985 --> 01:30:42,955
...Aygül, daughter of Dündar as your wife?

861
01:30:46,985 --> 01:30:48,335
I do.

862
01:30:48,415 --> 01:30:50,185
-Do you?
-I do.

863
01:30:50,445 --> 01:30:52,455
-Do you?
-I do.

864
01:31:00,845 --> 01:31:03,175
Do you witness?

865
01:31:03,605 --> 01:31:04,995
We do.

866
01:31:11,985 --> 01:31:15,185
May your marriage be blessed.

867
01:31:15,565 --> 01:31:16,915
Amen.

868
01:31:17,875 --> 01:31:19,235
Amen.

869
01:31:20,535 --> 01:31:21,855
Al Fatiha!

870
01:31:42,325 --> 01:31:43,685
Come on.

871
01:32:18,335 --> 01:32:19,915
Alps!

872
01:32:19,945 --> 01:32:23,265
Take your swords out!
Come on!

873
01:32:36,935 --> 01:32:38,985
Cerkutay alp is great!

874
01:32:39,195 --> 01:32:42,565
-Also is his heart!
-What, brother?

875
01:32:45,865 --> 01:32:48,935
What did he do for Aygül Hatun?

876
01:32:49,115 --> 01:32:54,165
He brought apples from the other world!

877
01:32:54,245 --> 01:32:57,565
But he ate them all himself!

878
01:33:00,065 --> 01:33:01,715
For how long did he wait?

879
01:33:01,875 --> 01:33:03,915
Too long!

880
01:33:03,915 --> 01:33:06,155
But he met his dream!

881
01:33:06,805 --> 01:33:08,595
Did he break any hearts?

882
01:33:08,595 --> 01:33:11,595
Never!

883
01:33:11,595 --> 01:33:14,355
He married Aygül Hatun!

884
01:33:16,825 --> 01:33:20,615
Then, may Allah grant them happiness!

885
01:33:20,825 --> 01:33:21,925
Amen!

886
01:33:21,925 --> 01:33:26,295
May you grow old together!

887
01:33:55,985 --> 01:33:57,515
Brother.

888
01:33:57,845 --> 01:33:59,345
Where are you going?

889
01:34:12,015 --> 01:34:13,375
Boran!

890
01:34:14,675 --> 01:34:16,515
Hit the lute!

891
01:34:16,945 --> 01:34:18,535
As you order, my Bey!

892
01:34:42,455 --> 01:34:52,505
We wintered in the land of Rum,
we committed a lot of good and evil.

893
01:34:52,505 --> 01:34:57,475
Come, let's make peace,
if you remember, let's know.

894
01:34:57,475 --> 01:35:02,445
Our horse is saddled,
we blew Alhamdulillah.

895
01:35:02,445 --> 01:35:04,735
We blew Alhamdulillah.

896
01:35:04,735 --> 01:35:14,815
We wintered in the land of Rum,
we committed a lot of good and evil.

897
01:35:14,815 --> 01:35:19,765
We were resurrected, became spring,
we were startled, became a river

898
01:35:19,765 --> 01:35:24,785
We flowed, we filled the sea,
we overflowed Alhamdulillah.

899
01:35:24,785 --> 01:35:27,705
We overflowed Alhamdulillah.

900
01:35:37,045 --> 01:35:42,045
We wintered in the land of Rum,
we committed a lot of good and evil.

901
01:35:42,045 --> 01:35:47,075
Spring has come back,
we migrated Alhamdulillah.

902
01:35:47,075 --> 01:35:52,165
We became slaves to the deed
you worshiped.

903
01:35:52,165 --> 01:35:57,135
We were sluggish and raw,
we learned Alhamdulillah.

904
01:35:57,135 --> 01:35:59,685
We learned Alhamdulillah.

905
01:35:59,685 --> 01:36:04,415
We wintered in the land of Rum,
we committed a lot of good and evil.

906
01:36:04,605 --> 01:36:09,695
Spring has come back,
we migrated Alhamdulillah.

907
01:36:09,695 --> 01:36:14,435
We wintered in the land of Rum,
we committed a lot of good and evil.

908
01:36:14,605 --> 01:36:19,695
Spring has come back,
we migrated Alhamdulillah.

909
01:36:19,695 --> 01:36:24,735
We migrated Alhamdulillah.
We migrated Alhamdulillah.

910
01:36:27,135 --> 01:36:28,865
Praise be!

911
01:36:29,495 --> 01:36:32,695
When we get to our tribe,
we will throw our arrow...

912
01:36:33,405 --> 01:36:36,715
...and build our home on the best place
of the tribe.

913
01:36:37,245 --> 01:36:38,775
I hope.

914
01:36:41,805 --> 01:36:43,845
You just return home safely.

915
01:36:46,025 --> 01:36:48,075
We will do all of them one by one...

916
01:36:49,495 --> 01:36:51,005
...my Cerkutay.

917
01:36:52,405 --> 01:36:55,245
What did you say?

918
01:36:56,745 --> 01:36:58,535
Did you say it to me?

919
01:36:58,735 --> 01:37:00,875
I couldn't hear. Say it again.

920
01:37:02,385 --> 01:37:03,955
Cerkutay!

921
01:37:11,675 --> 01:37:13,875
-Welcome.
-Thank you.

922
01:37:13,875 --> 01:37:15,455
Osman Bey is waiting for you.

923
01:37:15,885 --> 01:37:18,945
-Where is the assembly?
-I couldn't understand this.

924
01:37:19,715 --> 01:37:21,435
First, the place changed.

925
01:37:21,615 --> 01:37:23,335
Now, you brought us to the woods.

926
01:37:23,545 --> 01:37:25,845
Osman Bey doesn't do all this in vain.

927
01:37:26,445 --> 01:37:28,235
You will find out when you meet him.

928
01:37:28,595 --> 01:37:30,615
Where is Osman Bey?

929
01:37:31,625 --> 01:37:33,335
Now I will take you to him.

930
01:37:34,395 --> 01:37:35,915
But first...

931
01:37:36,715 --> 01:37:38,215
...Alps.

932
01:37:42,655 --> 01:37:46,245
Osman Bey's order. Cover the Bey's eyes.

933
01:38:40,115 --> 01:38:42,835
Go to Söğüt at once.
Find Vizier Alemşah.

934
01:38:42,835 --> 01:38:44,835
Convey my words to him.
Come on!

935
01:38:47,845 --> 01:38:50,075
We will attack when...

936
01:38:50,675 --> 01:38:52,075
...the poison takes effect.

937
01:38:52,385 --> 01:38:54,145
Come on, to the horses!

938
01:39:15,065 --> 01:39:17,585
Welcome, I am glad you came.

939
01:39:24,845 --> 01:39:26,845
We are not welcome at all, Osman Bey.

940
01:39:28,445 --> 01:39:30,185
What is this?

941
01:39:30,205 --> 01:39:34,005
Why did you put us through
all the trouble?

942
01:39:36,045 --> 01:39:38,975
I hope you have a reasonable excuse,
Osman Bey.

943
01:39:48,915 --> 01:39:50,935
Bless your right.

944
01:39:54,025 --> 01:39:56,115
But it is for precaution.

945
01:39:58,025 --> 01:40:00,815
What precaution?
Isn't this assembly secret?

946
01:40:01,575 --> 01:40:03,345
No other than the beys know about it.

947
01:40:03,785 --> 01:40:05,525
We thought so.

948
01:40:07,425 --> 01:40:09,135
But someone among us...

949
01:40:10,125 --> 01:40:14,515
...informed the Vizier about the assembly
and the place.

950
01:40:17,075 --> 01:40:18,615
Therefore...

951
01:40:20,975 --> 01:40:23,275
...there is a traitor among us.

952
01:40:29,035 --> 01:40:30,355
Who is it?

953
01:40:30,385 --> 01:40:34,125
Who betrays at this time can have no
dignity.

954
01:40:38,415 --> 01:40:40,605
How can there be a traitor among us?

955
01:41:11,590 --> 01:41:14,380
I would protect you, Commander
Geyhatu.

956
01:41:15,210 --> 01:41:17,210
Did we really need them?

957
01:41:36,490 --> 01:41:37,880
They...

958
01:41:39,810 --> 01:41:41,560
...die!

959
01:41:44,620 --> 01:41:46,450
If I tell them to.

960
01:41:47,670 --> 01:41:50,710
They don't ask questions like you...

961
01:41:51,290 --> 01:41:52,660
...Mingiyan.

962
01:41:58,070 --> 01:42:02,940
Mingiyan, what we need to prove is not
the value.

963
01:42:10,870 --> 01:42:14,020
They only follow the orders.

964
01:42:17,180 --> 01:42:19,530
You can't buy them...

965
01:42:20,430 --> 01:42:21,930
...or deceive them.

966
01:42:47,430 --> 01:42:48,740
Osman...

967
01:42:49,800 --> 01:42:52,800
...I am bringing you the death!

968
01:42:54,340 --> 01:42:56,400
With ninety-nine names of
Almighty Allah...

969
01:42:57,030 --> 01:43:07,050
...who makes us be when he says be, and
fills our hearts with the light of faith.

970
01:43:08,480 --> 01:43:10,760
In the name of Allah.

971
01:43:11,650 --> 01:43:14,270
In the name of Allah.

972
01:43:16,270 --> 01:43:22,330
I wish we could have our assembly in the
Bey Tribe, in Söğüt.

973
01:43:24,130 --> 01:43:29,270
But, you know the situation well.

974
01:43:31,550 --> 01:43:34,280
My Bey, you say there is a traitor
among us.

975
01:43:34,620 --> 01:43:36,330
But you still did the assembly.

976
01:43:36,400 --> 01:43:38,780
Aren't you afraid of what the traitor
will hear?

977
01:43:39,760 --> 01:43:40,980
On the contrary!

978
01:43:41,740 --> 01:43:46,880
I am glad he will convey what we will
declare beforehand.

979
01:43:52,010 --> 01:43:55,010
He should know.
He should know...

980
01:43:56,160 --> 01:43:59,730
...what happens to a traitor.

981
01:44:02,680 --> 01:44:04,010
Now...

982
01:44:05,610 --> 01:44:07,480
...you all must have heard.

983
01:44:09,040 --> 01:44:13,260
The tribes in the middle are rebelling.

984
01:44:15,870 --> 01:44:17,440
Then what we must do...

985
01:44:19,060 --> 01:44:21,770
...is uniting under that flag.

986
01:44:22,090 --> 01:44:26,820
Thus, we will support the rebellions
in faraway tribes.

987
01:44:28,530 --> 01:44:31,900
Osman Bey, Konya is listening to
every order of the Mongols.

988
01:44:32,340 --> 01:44:35,480
Rebelling to Geyhatu means
rebelling to the State.

989
01:44:36,470 --> 01:44:40,370
When was the last time you went to Konya,
Teymur Bey?

990
01:44:40,720 --> 01:44:42,810
I just came from Konya.

991
01:44:43,520 --> 01:44:46,430
Konya isn't listening to the Mongols.

992
01:44:48,660 --> 01:44:51,410
Konya now belongs to the Mongols.

993
01:44:54,310 --> 01:44:56,660
Is there a free state that we must fear...

994
01:44:56,850 --> 01:44:58,330
...a rebellion?

995
01:44:59,430 --> 01:45:01,260
You talk nice Osman Bey but...

996
01:45:01,320 --> 01:45:05,840
...your recent policies reduced
all the tribe's strength.

997
01:45:06,100 --> 01:45:07,530
What do we have that...

998
01:45:08,020 --> 01:45:09,530
...we can rebel with?

999
01:45:10,150 --> 01:45:15,920
We conducted that policy so that nothing
gets worse.

1000
01:45:17,420 --> 01:45:22,430
But there were those who believed
the tyrants.

1001
01:45:23,850 --> 01:45:25,140
Those who lost their ways.

1002
01:45:26,580 --> 01:45:30,670
Now the worse times came.

1003
01:45:32,010 --> 01:45:34,030
We are now in the end.

1004
01:45:34,730 --> 01:45:36,720
Now, the swords that are taken out...

1005
01:45:36,720 --> 01:45:39,970
...for the order of the world
are in charge.

1006
01:45:43,330 --> 01:45:48,450
There are experienced beys among you.

1007
01:45:51,940 --> 01:45:56,460
They know me very well and my father
Ertuğrul Gazi.

1008
01:45:58,690 --> 01:46:03,730
Thus, they don't say a word to me.

1009
01:46:05,660 --> 01:46:08,700
They do not object to anything.

1010
01:46:12,240 --> 01:46:13,560
They know that...

1011
01:46:15,250 --> 01:46:18,320
...Kayı never breaks his promise.

1012
01:46:18,920 --> 01:46:24,960
Now If there is anyone who is afraid of
rebellion, wants to escape the battle...

1013
01:46:26,290 --> 01:46:29,880
...he can wait to die in his tent.

1014
01:46:36,700 --> 01:46:38,850
I have one hundred tents in my tribe.

1015
01:46:42,090 --> 01:46:46,540
My tribe, my alps and my life...

1016
01:46:47,020 --> 01:46:49,610
...we are at your disposal.

1017
01:46:51,070 --> 01:46:52,590
Our way is...

1018
01:46:54,770 --> 01:46:56,510
...your way from now on, Osman Bey.

1019
01:46:58,460 --> 01:46:59,840
Thank you.

1020
01:47:05,270 --> 01:47:08,330
There are more soldiers to come...

1021
01:47:08,610 --> 01:47:10,650
...besides Geyhatu's army.

1022
01:47:13,550 --> 01:47:17,450
Argun Khan is sending
twenty thousand soldiers.

1023
01:47:28,920 --> 01:47:33,530
Osman, you knew I was coming!

1024
01:47:34,150 --> 01:47:35,950
But how?

1025
01:47:38,140 --> 01:47:40,140
Can I come in, my Vizier?

1026
01:47:44,690 --> 01:47:46,420
Come in, Konur.

1027
01:47:54,040 --> 01:47:55,360
You get out.

1028
01:48:13,010 --> 01:48:14,990
Güngör Bey poisoned the Nökers.

1029
01:48:15,790 --> 01:48:17,830
He is going after Geyhatu.

1030
01:48:18,900 --> 01:48:21,540
Geyhatu is going to the Kuzgun Hill.

1031
01:48:31,230 --> 01:48:33,510
Geyhatu!

1032
01:48:34,820 --> 01:48:39,480
Do you think I would give these lands to
the Mongols?

1033
01:48:41,810 --> 01:48:46,340
If there is a need for a leader, I will
be that leader.

1034
01:48:47,200 --> 01:48:50,230
You will burn in hell.

1035
01:48:50,830 --> 01:48:55,350
Your fire will be plenty because of the
slaughters you made.

1036
01:48:57,150 --> 01:48:59,740
My tribe has one hundred twenty tents,
Osman Bey.

1037
01:48:59,990 --> 01:49:02,840
Even if young people fight...

1038
01:49:02,930 --> 01:49:05,180
...only two hundred soldiers
will come out.

1039
01:49:05,240 --> 01:49:08,410
My horse is without saddle,
my arrow is without resentment.

1040
01:49:08,630 --> 01:49:11,950
Two hundred soldiers will fight with
honor beside us.

1041
01:49:13,050 --> 01:49:14,950
If Geyhatu passes us...

1042
01:49:16,280 --> 01:49:18,610
...he will destroy your tribe.

1043
01:49:20,280 --> 01:49:23,190
If you need it, both the sword
and the soldier will be found.

1044
01:49:26,980 --> 01:49:28,300
Master Davut.

1045
01:49:32,200 --> 01:49:33,530
Welcome.

1046
01:49:48,700 --> 01:49:52,430
Master Davut is preparing with his
blacksmiths...

1047
01:49:55,640 --> 01:49:58,510
...day and night.

1048
01:50:02,980 --> 01:50:05,230
We saw it all.

1049
01:50:05,460 --> 01:50:09,170
Thus, we made all the preparations.

1050
01:50:11,280 --> 01:50:12,790
Don't worry.

1051
01:50:13,520 --> 01:50:15,740
We have everything we need.

1052
01:50:17,740 --> 01:50:19,110
But...

1053
01:50:19,530 --> 01:50:24,590
...you must have heart, Beys!

1054
01:50:26,430 --> 01:50:29,970
You will encourage your hatuns,
your people.

1055
01:50:31,370 --> 01:50:34,210
You will be the strongest!

1056
01:50:34,570 --> 01:50:37,420
We came to make these lands home.

1057
01:50:37,790 --> 01:50:42,310
We have come to make Islam dominant
in these lands.

1058
01:50:46,260 --> 01:50:53,110
If we are to surrender without a fight
to the last drop of our blood...

1059
01:50:54,500 --> 01:50:57,710
...may the sky turn red!

1060
01:50:59,420 --> 01:51:00,570
Inshallah!

1061
01:51:04,320 --> 01:51:08,950
My tribe will provide five hundred
soldiers including the women.

1062
01:51:11,930 --> 01:51:16,560
I'm with you with three hundred horsemen
and two hundred pedestrians.

1063
01:51:18,880 --> 01:51:20,200
We are few...

1064
01:51:20,980 --> 01:51:23,050
...we don't fear death!

1065
01:51:23,250 --> 01:51:26,240
They must fear us!
We are with you, Osman Bey!

1066
01:51:26,860 --> 01:51:31,030
Thank you.
Thank you.

1067
01:51:32,500 --> 01:51:34,590
These lands are ours!

1068
01:51:36,290 --> 01:51:39,570
This place will be a home for those
who come friendly...

1069
01:51:39,570 --> 01:51:43,015
...and a grave for those
who come unfriendly.

1070
01:51:46,030 --> 01:51:48,090
May our battle be blessed!

1071
01:51:48,090 --> 01:51:49,650
Amen!

1072
01:52:06,160 --> 01:52:07,950
I am leaving now.

1073
01:52:09,850 --> 01:52:12,990
No, don't.

1074
01:52:13,870 --> 01:52:15,610
Don't.

1075
01:52:18,760 --> 01:52:20,840
You are my guests today.

1076
01:52:22,760 --> 01:52:24,400
There was a double assembly today.

1077
01:52:24,890 --> 01:52:29,810
Thus, we have a lot of meat and ayran.

1078
01:52:31,680 --> 01:52:34,570
Enjoy them.

1079
01:52:36,190 --> 01:52:39,670
But that traitor...

1080
01:52:41,040 --> 01:52:42,940
...will be found.

1081
01:52:47,530 --> 01:52:48,950
Now I am going to the battle.

1082
01:52:49,900 --> 01:52:55,180
Every sword I slash will come out of
this tent.

1083
01:52:56,000 --> 01:52:58,010
May your road be open, Osman Bey!

1084
01:52:58,520 --> 01:53:00,250
May your sword be sharp!

1085
01:53:00,320 --> 01:53:03,030
May your road be open and
your sword be sharp!

1086
01:53:03,120 --> 01:53:04,670
May your sword be sharp!

1087
01:53:05,480 --> 01:53:06,840
Thank you.

1088
01:53:09,320 --> 01:53:11,370
Thank you.

1089
01:53:30,790 --> 01:53:35,350
With my Allah's will, this will end today.

1090
01:53:52,370 --> 01:53:57,530
For the sake of the oppressed, my sword
will cut the neck of the oppressor!

1091
01:53:57,530 --> 01:54:01,070
May your road be open!
We will be praying for you!

1092
01:54:01,230 --> 01:54:03,320
May your sword be sharp, my Bey!

1093
01:54:03,440 --> 01:54:05,950
Be careful, my valiants!

1094
01:54:05,950 --> 01:54:07,500
Thank you, mother!

1095
01:54:37,810 --> 01:54:39,840
May Allah be with you, my Cerkutay.

1096
01:54:44,580 --> 01:54:45,920
Ayşe.

1097
01:55:02,090 --> 01:55:06,080
Aygül, why do you look sad?

1098
01:55:08,230 --> 01:55:11,960
You suffered a lot, now it's time to
be happy.

1099
01:55:12,580 --> 01:55:15,810
Don't forget your promise.
Don't be upset.

1100
01:55:17,350 --> 01:55:19,380
Even if you are upset...

1101
01:55:19,380 --> 01:55:22,140
...Cerkutay will find a way
to make you smile.

1102
01:55:23,700 --> 01:55:25,490
Thank you, mother.

1103
01:55:28,670 --> 01:55:30,460
I just got overwhelmed.

1104
01:55:32,520 --> 01:55:34,560
Keep your heart relaxed, my girl.

1105
01:55:34,750 --> 01:55:37,800
They will return safe and sound.

1106
01:55:40,230 --> 01:55:44,020
I hope.
I hope.

1107
01:55:44,520 --> 01:55:45,840
Come on.

1108
01:56:59,380 --> 01:57:01,100
Welcome, Kosses.

1109
01:57:24,770 --> 01:57:27,540
I've been in this castle
ever since I can remember.

1110
01:57:28,240 --> 01:57:29,740
Gündüz Bey.

1111
01:57:31,370 --> 01:57:32,700
Welcome to you.

1112
01:57:57,530 --> 01:58:01,620
I got this castle from your friend,
Nikola.

1113
01:58:03,300 --> 01:58:04,800
Not from you.

1114
01:58:06,500 --> 01:58:10,340
A took it with blood.

1115
01:58:19,950 --> 01:58:23,500
Right, I forgot.

1116
01:58:25,570 --> 01:58:27,920
You and Nikola are the same.

1117
01:58:29,970 --> 01:58:34,380
You are those who stab
their friends on their backs.

1118
01:58:36,800 --> 01:58:40,630
I never did.

1119
01:58:43,340 --> 01:58:47,290
What happened with my brother doesn't
concern you.

1120
01:58:48,770 --> 01:58:50,140
Know your place.

1121
01:58:52,400 --> 01:58:54,860
Your visit is over...

1122
01:58:56,540 --> 01:58:58,510
...Gündüz Bey.

1123
01:58:59,310 --> 01:59:04,320
I can't do anything to you right now
because of the situation.

1124
01:59:07,950 --> 01:59:11,950
Pray that you've been a friend
to my brother.

1125
01:59:15,220 --> 01:59:16,650
You can leave.

1126
01:59:21,870 --> 01:59:24,610
We will meet again, Kosses.

1127
01:59:27,920 --> 01:59:29,710
Come on, Valiants!

1128
02:00:02,470 --> 02:00:03,820
Soldiers!

1129
02:00:09,090 --> 02:00:13,490
Osman chose a decent place for himself.

1130
02:00:14,520 --> 02:00:16,550
This place sees everywhere.

1131
02:00:16,780 --> 02:00:18,820
It is safe from ambushes.

1132
02:00:19,430 --> 02:00:23,380
But this time, we are superior
than nature.

1133
02:00:23,930 --> 02:00:27,300
The first to come claims his enemy.

1134
02:00:36,580 --> 02:00:39,800
Bravo! Scholar Geyhatu, bravo!

1135
02:00:43,590 --> 02:00:45,720
You are correct.

1136
02:00:46,520 --> 02:00:49,770
But there is a slight incorrectness.

1137
02:00:50,600 --> 02:00:54,480
Because we were here first.

1138
02:00:56,740 --> 02:01:03,840
And Rogatus Laskaris,
from Laskaris Dynasty!

1139
02:01:15,290 --> 02:01:17,030
What happened, Geyhatu?

1140
02:01:17,050 --> 02:01:19,300
You look like you have seen a ghost!

1141
02:01:24,730 --> 02:01:28,420
He is pale, because he knows he is
living his last day.

1142
02:01:28,620 --> 02:01:30,480
I can't even see his eyes.

1143
02:01:31,860 --> 02:01:34,650
Lords talk well.

1144
02:01:35,740 --> 02:01:38,600
Their tongue works well.

1145
02:01:40,480 --> 02:01:44,710
However, their head doesn't work.

1146
02:01:46,130 --> 02:01:52,410
So you are going to die
with Osman.

1147
02:01:54,020 --> 02:01:55,780
I am at ease.

1148
02:02:01,420 --> 02:02:03,730
Your end will be harsh.

1149
02:02:11,860 --> 02:02:18,080
But your job at the other world
is even harsher.

1150
02:02:31,730 --> 02:02:34,200
Your grave waits for you Geyhatu.

1151
02:02:39,550 --> 02:02:43,010
Is this how you protect the
future of Turks, Osman?

1152
02:02:43,010 --> 02:02:44,300
What a shame.

1153
02:02:45,740 --> 02:02:49,510
Can a Bey who works with a Lord
found a state?

1154
02:02:50,310 --> 02:02:55,370
You united and trapped me.

1155
02:03:01,940 --> 02:03:04,220
Rogatus wake up!

1156
02:03:18,090 --> 02:03:20,720
I set up such a game that...

1157
02:03:21,940 --> 02:03:24,850
...you are not going to get rid of it.

1158
02:03:25,100 --> 02:03:30,760
You cannot corner someone who was born
on the horse, Osman.

1159
02:03:31,160 --> 02:03:33,350
We were born on the horse too!

1160
02:03:34,180 --> 02:03:36,220
We ate meat...

1161
02:03:36,440 --> 02:03:38,460
We rided horses.

1162
02:03:40,400 --> 02:03:42,980
But we have a supremacy against you.

1163
02:03:45,210 --> 02:03:48,220
We have been honored with Islam.

1164
02:03:54,340 --> 02:03:58,130
Then you are going to die with your honor.

1165
02:03:58,820 --> 02:04:04,200
We are as large as the world, Osman.

1166
02:04:05,430 --> 02:04:10,120
There is no land that doesn't belong
to Genghis Khan.

1167
02:04:10,120 --> 02:04:12,780
Every land waits for its time.

1168
02:04:12,990 --> 02:04:15,920
Until you face us.

1169
02:04:18,580 --> 02:04:20,530
You are going to die.

1170
02:04:20,990 --> 02:04:23,350
And the ones who follow you too.

1171
02:04:23,780 --> 02:04:27,190
The dominance of this world
is Turks'!

1172
02:04:28,620 --> 02:04:31,670
You can't even protect what you have.

1173
02:04:31,670 --> 02:04:35,400
How can you set your eyes on the world?

1174
02:04:35,860 --> 02:04:38,130
I don't trust what I have in my hands...

1175
02:04:42,450 --> 02:04:44,500
I trust what I have in my heart.

1176
02:04:45,380 --> 02:04:50,080
Samarkand, Konya, even Otuken

1177
02:04:50,590 --> 02:04:56,160
The breed of Genghis rules
everywhere you think yours.

1178
02:04:56,380 --> 02:05:02,680
God lives in the time.
Humans were born to die.

1179
02:05:07,480 --> 02:05:10,560
Do not forget the lose you had.

1180
02:05:12,520 --> 02:05:14,980
You are not as strong as before.

1181
02:05:14,980 --> 02:05:18,440
I neither die with a trap...

1182
02:05:18,800 --> 02:05:22,540
Nor Mongols wipe out with a lose.

1183
02:05:36,590 --> 02:05:39,630
The poison is kicking in.

1184
02:06:21,890 --> 02:06:26,080
Osman, you proved your cowardness.

1185
02:06:27,690 --> 02:06:32,180
You poisoned the ones whom
you cannot beat.

1186
02:06:40,990 --> 02:06:50,510
However, if you kill me, 20,000 Mongol
soldiers will destroy you.

1187
02:06:53,830 --> 02:06:56,870
Everyone who is trying to stop my brother
is here.

1188
02:06:56,870 --> 02:06:59,270
Mongols will fall one by one.

1189
02:06:59,480 --> 02:07:01,360
What can I want more?

1190
02:07:01,970 --> 02:07:04,150
Come on valiants, let's go.

1191
02:07:04,900 --> 02:07:07,350
Attack!

1192
02:07:30,160 --> 02:07:33,230
So you poisoned the soldiers.

1193
02:07:33,650 --> 02:07:36,800
I would poison you too Osman...

1194
02:07:37,000 --> 02:07:39,610
...if I had known you were working with
the Lords!

1195
02:07:46,670 --> 02:07:49,010
Soldiers, get ready!

1196
02:07:52,450 --> 02:07:57,030
Allah is eternal!

1197
02:09:04,800 --> 02:09:06,030
Alps!

1198
02:09:06,860 --> 02:09:09,910
Follow Geyhatu! Come on!

1199
02:09:10,950 --> 02:09:12,740
Come on hurry!

1200
02:09:23,170 --> 02:09:25,700
Osman Bey follows Geyhatu.

1201
02:09:25,730 --> 02:09:27,230
We'll kill them.

1202
02:09:43,350 --> 02:09:44,920
Geyhatu!

1203
02:09:49,350 --> 02:09:51,650
Where are you running Geyhatu?

1204
02:09:52,160 --> 02:09:53,750
Attack!

1205
02:10:41,510 --> 02:10:44,390
A Sultan should kill Geyhatu!

1206
02:10:44,390 --> 02:10:46,160
Who the hell are you, shepherd?

1207
02:11:33,130 --> 02:11:34,920
Here is your death.

1208
02:11:34,970 --> 02:11:37,090
You are going to die Geyhatu.

1209
02:11:41,090 --> 02:11:42,610
You will die in pain.

1210
02:12:29,130 --> 02:12:30,930
My Bey!

1211
02:12:48,310 --> 02:12:50,470
Let me help my Bey.

1212
02:13:04,920 --> 02:13:08,260
Geyhatu, your turn will come too!

1213
02:13:49,250 --> 02:13:50,770
Who are you?

1214
02:13:51,470 --> 02:13:53,580
Who are you serving?

1215
02:13:53,750 --> 02:13:56,530
I care the future of Turks!

1216
02:13:57,450 --> 02:13:59,480
You were the one who worked with Vizier...

1217
02:14:00,320 --> 02:14:03,650
...and tried to kill Beys who didn't obey.

1218
02:14:05,430 --> 02:14:08,510
Do you care the future of Turks
by killing them?

1219
02:14:08,670 --> 02:14:12,310
I will crush everyone until
I get to my objective!

1220
02:14:16,430 --> 02:14:18,030
What is your objective.

1221
02:14:18,390 --> 02:14:20,770
It is to kill you for now, Osman.

1222
02:14:23,200 --> 02:14:24,590
Come.

1223
02:14:24,590 --> 02:14:26,670
Attack!

1224
02:14:27,410 --> 02:14:29,200
Ya Allah!

1225
02:14:47,520 --> 02:14:49,790
Geyhatu.

1226
02:15:26,730 --> 02:15:28,050
Rogatus.

1227
02:15:29,320 --> 02:15:30,590
Rogatus.

1228
02:15:34,090 --> 02:15:35,590
Boran alp.

1229
02:15:36,760 --> 02:15:38,810
I am sorry for your wife.

1230
02:15:42,060 --> 02:15:49,410
Osman Bey, I am dying for real this time.

1231
02:15:52,890 --> 02:15:54,020
But...

1232
02:15:54,990 --> 02:15:58,810
My heart is fresh.
I am on the right side.

1233
02:16:17,780 --> 02:16:19,170
Geyhatu.

1234
02:16:21,100 --> 02:16:22,450
Geyhatu.

1235
02:16:26,190 --> 02:16:27,730
Where is Geyhatu?

1236
02:16:27,730 --> 02:16:29,950
We are here to kill Geyhatu!
Where is he?

1237
02:16:29,950 --> 02:16:32,049
Of course! He saw us.

1238
02:16:32,150 --> 02:16:33,689
He must die now.

1239
02:16:33,689 --> 02:16:35,809
- Let's find him!
- Come on!

1240
02:16:35,809 --> 02:16:37,160
Hurry!

1241
02:16:45,250 --> 02:16:48,009
Turgut Bey! Follow Geyhatu!

1242
02:17:12,490 --> 02:17:14,030
Turgut Bey!

1243
02:17:17,429 --> 02:17:19,469
No one shall leave!

1244
02:17:19,709 --> 02:17:22,080
We have things to settle!

1245
02:17:49,740 --> 02:17:52,280
Vizier.

1246
02:17:56,439 --> 02:17:59,240
Vizier.

1247
02:17:59,760 --> 02:18:11,770
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com